Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:35:21 +0200
Subject: [M152] [maglev] Only materialize hole NaNs as the_hole in
 FixedDoubleArray

Original change's description:
> [maglev] Only materialize hole NaNs as the_hole in FixedDoubleArray
>
> In Maglev and Turbolev virtual object deopt translation, Float64Constant
> values with the hole-NaN bit pattern were translated to the_hole_value
> for all virtual object slots, rather than only FixedDoubleArray
> elements. If a Float64Constant with the hole-NaN bit pattern flowed
> into a tagged slot (such as a PACKED_ELEMENTS FixedArray) or a captured
> HeapNumber, deopt materialization wrote the_hole_value instead of a
> HeapNumber.
>
> Pass the enclosing VirtualObject to BuildNestedValue and
> AddVirtualObjectNestedValue and restrict the hole-NaN and undefined-NaN
> deopt literal translation to FixedDoubleArray virtual objects so that
> Float64Constant nodes in other virtual objects always reify to a
> HeapNumber.
>
> Drive-by: implement the TODO(nicohartmann) for handling
> is_undefined_nan() in MaglevFrameTranslationBuilder::BuildNestedValue,
> and relax the hole-NaN DCHECK in
> JSObjectRef::GetOwnFastConstantDoubleProperty when
> --expose-memory-corruption-api is enabled.
>
